import Thomson.Pivots.Residual

/-! # Task 1b, step 8: `N`

`N` is the 17-digit approximate inverse of `pivotMatrix` from `scripts/threepoint/task1_design.json`
(`approx_inverse`), exact on the `10⁻⁴⁰` grid — with its first column halved.  `task1_leanform.py`
builds the bound row as *half* of `28a₀ − 4a₁ − 4F − E`, believing that to be `evalRow .bound`; but
`(64a₀ − 8(a₀+a₁) − 8F)/2 = 28a₀ − 4a₁ − 4F`, so `pivotMatrix`'s bound row is twice the one
inverted (its first column is `−4·Gh j (1,1,1)`, `pivotMatrix_bound_row`), and `N·pivotMatrix` is
`diag(2, 1, …, 1)` until the column is halved.  All other rows agree.

The table is a nested *list*, row by row: the kernel reduces `List.getD` but not the well-founded
recursion behind `Array.ofFn`, and the whole check is now kernel work (`KCol00`–`KCol23`,
`KRes`, `Check`). -/

